don't see any practical use for the query that\r\n\r\n```typescript\r\n.whereInIds([1, 2, 3])\r\n.andWhere('x = 1')\r\n```\r\n\r\nproduces.\r\n\r\nEspecially if we consider SQL IN query. Consider the following table:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndb=# select * from items;\r\n id | x\r\n----+---\r\n  1 | 1\r\n  2 | 1\r\n  3 | NULL\r\n  4 | NULL\r\n(4 rows)\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow perform the query I would expect `.whereInIds([3, 2]).andWhere('x = 1')` to do:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndb=# select * from items where id in (3, 2) and x = 1;\r\n id | x\r\n----+---\r\n  2 | 1\r\n(1 row)\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut, the query performed by TypeORM 0.2 is:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndb=# select * from items where (id = 3) or (id = 2) and x = 1;\r\n id | x\r\n----+---\r\n  2 | 1\r\n  3 | NULL\r\n(2 rows)\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo me this looks like a bug, but if it's not I can live with it since `where('x = 1').andWhereInIds([3, 2])` performs the query I need:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndb=# select * from items where x = 1 and ((id = 3) or (id = 2));\r\n id | x\r\n----+---\r\n  2 | 1\r\n(1 row)\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/typeorm/typeorm/issues/comments/387680042/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"vesse","id":738763,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczODc2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/738763?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse","html_url":"https://github.com/vesse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vesse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/v